<section class="section">
  <div class="container prose" style="max-width:var(--max-prose)">
    <p style="padding:1.25rem;background:var(--bg-alt);border-left:3px solid var(--gold-500);border-radius:0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;margin-bottom:2rem"><strong>Reference copy.</strong> This is the template of our service agreement; not a contract you sign here. Your actual, countersigned version will arrive by email after your discovery call.</p>

    <h2>1. The parties</h2>
    <p>This agreement is between <strong>Pikes Peak Web Designs</strong> (referred to as "we" or "us"), a Colorado-based web design studio, and the <strong>Client</strong> (you), an individual or business entity engaging us to design, build, and maintain a website.</p>

    <h2>2. Scope of services</h2>
    <p>Under the <strong>Monthly Plan</strong>, we agree to provide:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Custom, hand-coded website design and development (up to 10 content pages)</li>
      <li>Eight operational pages included at no cost and outside the 10-page count: Privacy Policy, Accessibility Statement, Terms of Use, Contact page, Thank-You page, Testimonials page, Style Guide, and Sitemap</li>
      <li>Standard build features: light and dark mode with system-preference detection, responsive header and navigation, accessible mobile hamburger menu, built-in Pagefind search, privacy-focused analytics, WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility, and CDN-served performance</li>
      <li>Technical infrastructure files: robots.txt, humans.txt, security.txt, sitemap.xml, RSS feed (when applicable), 404 page, favicon suite, and Open Graph / Twitter images</li>
      <li>Website hosting on a fast global CDN with SSL</li>
      <li>Unlimited content updates during the term of the agreement</li>
      <li>24/7 emergency support for site-down or site-critical issues</li>
      <li>On-page SEO foundation (meta, schema, sitemap, structured headings)</li>
      <li>Ongoing security monitoring and maintenance</li>
      <li>A visual refresh every 24 months during the term</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Under the <strong>Lump-Sum Plan</strong>, we agree to deliver a custom, hand-coded website of up to 10 content pages plus the eight operational pages, with full code ownership transferred to you on delivery. Ongoing hosting, updates, and support are separate optional services.</p>

    <h2>3. Fees &amp; payment</h2>
    <p><strong>Monthly Plan:</strong> $175 USD per month (or equivalent in CAD), billed on the same calendar day each month, with a 12-month minimum term. After 12 months, the agreement converts to month-to-month with 30 days' written notice to cancel.</p>
    <p><strong>Lump-Sum Plan:</strong> $4,000 USD (or equivalent in CAD), with 50% due on project kickoff and 50% due on launch.</p>
    <p><strong>Add-ons:</strong> Extra content pages beyond the included ten are $150 each, one-time. A blog section is a $200 one-time add-on.</p>
    <p>All prices exclude applicable sales tax. Payments are processed via secure card or ACH.</p>

    <h2>4. Timeline</h2>
    <p>Our target is to design, build, and launch your site within 2–3 weeks of the discovery call, provided you can deliver basic content (logo, photos, services list) in the first week. We commit to doing our part; timelines that slip due to client delays are not our responsibility but we'll keep you informed either way.</p>

    <h2>5. Client responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide accurate, honest information about your business</li>
      <li>Review and approve designs within a reasonable timeframe</li>
      <li>Keep your account current and respond to payment issues promptly</li>
      <li>Not ask us to build anything illegal, defamatory, or infringing</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Our responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Deliver a custom-coded, accessible, fast website fit for your business</li>
      <li>Handle hosting, security, and maintenance (Monthly Plan) without extra billing</li>
      <li>Respond to content-update requests within one business day in most cases</li>
      <li>Respond to emergencies within an hour during business hours, same day on weekends</li>
      <li>Tell you, in plain language, when something is outside our scope or unreasonable</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Ownership</h2>
    <p><strong>Monthly Plan:</strong> We own the source code and host it on your behalf while the agreement is active. Your domain is always registered in your name and never ours. Your photos, text, and brand assets remain yours. If you want to move to code ownership later, we'll quote a reasonable buyout.</p>
    <p><strong>Lump-Sum Plan:</strong> Full code ownership transfers to you on final payment and delivery.</p>

    <h2>8. Cancellation</h2>
    <p><strong>Monthly Plan:</strong> After the 12-month minimum, either party may cancel with 30 days' written notice. Within the 12-month minimum, early cancellation by the client requires payment of the remaining monthly installments. We will not cancel the agreement on you without cause unless you violate these terms.</p>
    <p><strong>Lump-Sum Plan:</strong> Not applicable; this is a one-time engagement.</p>
    <p>At cancellation we will help you transition your domain to a registrar of your choice and export your content. On the Monthly Plan, the site itself comes offline unless we reach an alternate arrangement.</p>

    <h2>9. Confidentiality</h2>
    <p>Anything you share with us in confidence stays in confidence; including business strategy, pricing, internal documents, and customer data. We won't share your information with third parties except as required to deliver the services (e.g. your domain registrar, our hosting provider) or as required by law.</p>

    <h2>10. Warranties &amp; limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>We warrant that the work will be performed professionally and that the deliverables will be free of our negligent errors at the time of launch. We don't guarantee any particular search ranking, sales outcome, or business result; we guarantee our workmanship and our responsiveness.</p>
    <p>Our total liability under this agreement is limited to the fees paid by you in the 12 months preceding any claim.</p>

    <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
    <p>This agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Colorado, United States. Disputes will be resolved first through friendly discussion, then through mediation, and finally (if needed) in the state and federal courts located in El Paso County, Colorado.</p>

    <h2>12. Signatures</h2>
    <p>The version you sign will have signature blocks for both parties, dates, and specific terms for your plan and business. It arrives by email with e-signature support. No printing, scanning, or faxing required.</p>

    <hr>

    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted)">Questions about this agreement? <a href="/contact/" class="inline-link">Reach out</a>. We'd rather answer questions now than have surprises later.</p>
